{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551283-is-there-an-explanation-for-the-american-locust-in-lore","id":1551283,"title":"Is there an explanation for the american locust in lore?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-25T19:23:36-07:00","id":1551283,"title":"Is there an explanation for the american locust in lore?","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yNpZvJ4YIB4?si=E90n04qXbrPxyJG6\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yNpZvJ4YIB4?si=E90n04qXbrPxyJG6\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yNpZvJ4YIB4?si=E90n04qXbrPxyJG6\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/yNpZvJ4YIB4?si=E90n04qXbrPxyJG6 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Considering that the American Locust didn't appear until after the Europeans invaded it could imply that they showed up due to Europeans bringing Wyrm-corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 06-28-2025, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T23:22:39-07:00","id":1551287,"title":"","content":"By &quot;american locust&quot; do you just mean locust plagues in general? Because there are Old World locusts as well.<br /> <br /> There's no game lore about them because it's a natural phenomenon. Some grasshopper species (not all) have solitary and gregarious phases. Those that do sometimes swarm due to local weather conditions with devastating results.<br /> <br /> I don't think this has even been mentioned or addressed in sourcebooks. If you want, you could certainly tie certain locust plagues, as well as other natural disasters, to certain Wyrm spirits. But such things are also &quot;of Gaia&quot;. So you would want to distinguish between &quot;natural phenomenon&quot; (which while bad, is not anti-Gaian) and any corrupt manifestations of it (such as those that do not occur naturally, but only happen because of some Wyrm-influenced witchcraft).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T23:50:03-07:00","id":1551289,"title":"","content":"It's also generally a good idea to say something more than a question in the title and link to a video. Many people don't really trust blind links on the Internet even from regular posters on a forum.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why we'd need an explanation for the &quot;American locust&quot; in lore... as there are native locusts in the Americas, even if humans drove the most destructive species into extinction so locust swarms aren't as common place as they are in other parts of the world where they're still a major source of food insecurity.<br /> <br /> Though I think many Garou would attribute locusts to the Wyld more than the Wyrm; as many natural disasters are treated as Wyld affliated or Wyld adjacent in Garou cosmology (backed up with spirits such as Earthquake, Twister, and Volcano all being associated with the Wyld despite also serving as patrons to Gaian aligned Garou). The Bone Gnawers and Ratkin are no strangers to whipping up &quot;pest&quot; swarms either, and that's seen as being influenced by the Wyld as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T12:38:55-07:00","id":1553545,"title":"","content":"Well, I was just thinking since the natives blamed the White Man for the locusts since it never happened before, I would assume the Werewolves would associate them with the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T18:29:04-07:00","id":1553550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551283-is-there-an-explanation-for-the-american-locust-in-lore?p=1553545#post1553545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was just thinking since the natives blamed the White Man for the locusts since it never happened before, I would assume the Werewolves would associate them with the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find any source for this affirmation, that seems rather strange.<br /> <br /> Do you have anything at all about this besides this link?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-30T00:21:40-07:00","id":1553551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551283-is-there-an-explanation-for-the-american-locust-in-lore?p=1553545#post1553545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was just thinking since the natives blamed the White Man for the locusts since it never happened before, I would assume the Werewolves would associate them with the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that would hold up<br /> <b>Rocky Mountain locust</b> became a problem in the 19th century becasue farming expanded westward into the grasshoppers' favored habitat<br /> More so, the Rocky Mountain locust went extinct <i>because</i> of the destruction of its unique montane river valley breeding grounds by settlers in the late 1800s. Plowing, cultivation, irrigation, and grazing by livestock destroyed the specific soil and vegetation necessary for the locusts' eggs to hatch, which disrupted the species' ability to reproduce even during natural population recession<br /> So if anything the Wester settlers, &quot;white men&quot; and &quot; Wyrmcomers&quot; (other Garou from Europe) in a sense &quot;fixed&quot; the problem they caused in the first place in a very twisted and grotesque way<br /> The Rocky Mountain locust was present in America from prehistory, with evidence of its existence in the Late Pleistocene\u200b and they had swarms before just farming made it more severe... than made them extinct. \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}